     "cookies": [],
     "content": {
      "size": 2837,
      "mimeType": "application/json",
      "text": "{\"type\":\"standard\",\"title\":\"Beer snake\",\"displaytitle\":\"<span lang=\\\"en\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-page-title-main\\\">Beer snake</span></span>\",\"namespace\":{\"id\":0,\"text\":\"\"},\"wikibase_item\":\"Q4880039\",\"titles\":{\"canonical\":\"Beer_snake\",\"normalized\":\"Beer snake\",\"display\":\"<span lang=\\\"en\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-page-title-main\\\">Beer snake</span></span>\"},\"pageid\":4655446,\"thumbnail\":{\"source\":\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/SCG-Beersnake2004-01-04.jpg/330px-SCG-Beersnake2004-01-04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail\",\"width\":330,\"height\":277},\"originalimage\":{\"source\":\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/51/SCG-Beersnake2004-01-04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\",\"width\":803,\"height\":674},\"lang\":\"en\",\"dir\":\"ltr\",\"revision\":\"1381126585\",\"tid\":\"916c5d5b-cc3f-11f1-a999-2ac6e78f94d4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-20T04:34:42Z\",\"description\":\"Stacking of numerous plastic beer cups\",\"description_source\":\"local\",\"content_urls\":{\"desktop\":{\"page\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beer_snake\",\"revisions\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beer_snake?action=history\",\"edit\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beer_snake?action=edit\",\"talk\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Beer_snake\"},\"mobile\":{\"page\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beer_snake\",\"revisions\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Beer_snake\",\"edit\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beer_snake?action=edit\",\"talk\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Beer_snake\"}},\"extract\":\"A beer snake, or cup snake, is the stacking of numerous beer cups into a long, flexible structure that resembles a snake. Beer snakes are most commonly found at sporting events that are played out over many hours, such as cricket. Some snakes have been reported in the media as being up to 175 metres (574 ft) long. They are typically formed during breaks in play or when the outcome of the match is nearly certain; for example, when the fourth Test of the Pakistani cricket team in England in 2006 tour at The Oval was halted after ball-tampering allegations, a large beer snake was constructed in the OCS stand.\",\"extract_html\":\"<p>A <b>beer snake</b>, or <b>cup snake</b>, is the stacking of numerous beer cups into a long, flexible structure that resembles a snake. Beer snakes are most commonly found at sporting events that are played out over many hours, such as cricket. Some snakes have been reported in the media as being up to 175 metres (574 ft) long. They are typically formed during breaks in play or when the outcome of the match is nearly certain; for example, when the fourth Test of the Pakistani cricket team in England in 2006 tour at The Oval was halted after ball-tampering allegations, a large beer snake was constructed in the OCS stand.</p>\"}"
     },
     "redirectURL": "",
     "headersSize": -1,
     "bodySize": 2837
    },
